{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"transaction-submit-for-partial-settlement-node","reason":"Full C13 retrieval review ran from 2026-09-21T13:30:14Z to 2026-09-21T13:31:30Z UTC; final verdict: changes_requested. The complete primary raw supports the PayPal/Venmo-only availability statement, parent-authorization and per-portion child transactions, ordinary-settlement prohibition, callback/Promise result handling, damaged lifecycle rendering, child-only refund restrictions, and Control Panel linkage. The fully read supporting Submit For Settlement raw independently says multiple partial settlements are also available for some credit-card transactions for select merchants, so the candidate correctly treats this as an unresolved availability conflict and legitimately cites the supporting raw as distinct authority. Primary raw ownership remains unique. The candidate itself and proposed server-SDK route preserve the conflict, but two bounded promotion defects remain: the existing ordinary Submit For Settlement source states the broader availability without a reciprocal conflict warning/link to the dedicated partial-settlement source, and none of the five receipt quotes contains the supporting raw's select-merchant credit-card sentence even though the conflict-bearing reciprocal route cites all five quote indexes. A reader entering through the existing source can therefore receive an apparently universal broader eligibility answer, and the shared conflict wording is not fully quote-grounded."}
